    how: 'The hoover is a Juno-type voice pushed to extremes: sawtooth and square together, the square’s width swept by an LFO, an octave below mixed in, and heavy chorus. Here six voices are stacked on each note and detuned, and portamento makes the notes swoop into each other. The MOD envelope bends the pitch down at the start of every note, which gives the "whoop".',
